name: meditate
audience: private
description: >
  Recoverable consolidation of Claude and Codex behavioral directives from
  instruction files, agent memories, interaction evidence, and Kindex.

domains:
  - agent-state
  - instruction-hygiene
  - temporal-reasoning
  - llm-tooling
  - provenance

voice:
  tone: direct, evidence-led, and conservative around destructive changes
  principles:
    - Rewrite contradictory rules instead of appending another exception
    - Preserve temporal and source provenance for every promoted directive
    - Keep raw histories local and redact before any model call
    - Archive first and make every applied rewrite recoverable
    - Prefer deterministic evidence and explicit user corrections over agent inference
  anti-patterns:
    - Uploading raw transcripts to an LLM
    - Treating file modification time as proof of authority
    - Deleting old evidence merely because it is old
    - Silently rewriting live instructions
    - Claiming a clean consolidation when model or validation work failed

standards:
  code_review:
    - Apply is transactional, content-addressed, atomic, and restore-tested
    - Every model input passes local secret redaction first
    - Every output directive has evidence lineage and scope
    - Dry-run is the default; unattended apply requires explicit configuration
  testing:
    - Use synthetic Claude and Codex histories; never copy personal logs into fixtures
    - Cover conflict resolution, temporal ordering, redaction, TOCTOU, restore, and cron locking

connects_to:
  - kindex
  - advocate
  - constrain
  - simulacrum

work_policy:
  require_active_tag: false
  linear:
    enabled: false
    require_issue: false
  git:
    block_commit_without_tag: false
    block_commit_without_linear: false
    block_push_without_tag: false
    block_push_without_linear: false
